-- Evidence that itself takes evidence, so §6 eta-expands it — and the
-- closure names a function that has to have survived (`backend.md` §9;
-- `static-dispatch-spike.md` §8.2, A.25).
--
-- `Pair.eq` carries a `where` clause of its own, so §8.1 gives it a hidden
-- leading parameter and the bare name `DceEtaEvidence$eq` is a function of
-- the WRONG arity for an evidence slot. §6 therefore passes
-- `($p$1, $p$2) => DceEtaEvidence$eq(<inner evidence>, $p$1, $p$2)` — a
-- closure built out of the site's targets, which is exactly why §9 needs no
-- rule for eta-expansion: *an eta-expansion is built from a site's targets,
-- and the targets are the edges.*
--
-- **Every `==` here is written on a `Maybe` or on a record**, never on a
-- bare `Pair`, and that is what makes the fixture sharp. The site's own
-- target is `Maybe`'s derived `eq` (or the record shape's); this module's
-- `eq` is one level DOWN, inside that target's `parts` range, which is the
-- edge §9's walk only sees by recursing through `Dispatch.partsAt`. Nothing
-- in this file calls `eq` by name, no site names it, and `Bir.refs` has no
-- row for it — so without the recursion it is deleted, and the emitted
-- `Maybe$Maybe$$eq(($p$1, $p$2) => DceEtaEvidence$eq(…), x, y)` names a
-- `const` that is not there.
--
-- `Pair` compares its FIRST slot only, so a build that silently substituted
-- a structural walk would print the opposite on every line.
import Maybe exposing (Maybe)
import Node exposing (Program)


pub type Pair a
    = Pair a a


pub eq : Pair a, Pair a -> Bool
    where a.eq : a, a -> Bool
eq x y =
    case x of
        Pair firstX _ ->
            case y of
                Pair firstY _ ->
                    firstX == firstY


show : Bool -> String
show b =
    if b then
        "True"
    else
        "False"


main : Program
main =
    Node.printLines
        [ show (Just (Pair 1 2) == Just (Pair 1 9))
        , show (Just (Pair 1 2) == Just (Pair 7 2))
        , show (Just (Pair "a" "b") == Just (Pair "a" "z"))
        , show (Just (Pair 1 2) == Nothing)
        , show ({ item = Pair 1 2 } == { item = Pair 1 9 })
        ]
